      {
        "q": "Can I pay a relative's utility bill abroad with either one?",
        "a": "Xoom's <a href=\"https://www.xoom.com/user-agreement\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\">user agreement</a> offers Bill Pay for this: your relative is the beneficiary and the utility is the company that receives the money. You confirm that the beneficiary has agreed to you using their account information, such as a utility account number, and has allowed PayPal to collect and verify information about them. WorldRemit's <a href=\"https://assets.ctfassets.net/sb7j5o4oxtgv/38QndD6vN3PiIXYEzjS0Uq/6f0a02c5658ce80ff438a5917b7206ed/270326_ZepzTermsUS.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\">US terms</a> say to send only to people you know or trust, mention paying a utility bill as a commercial purpose the service may permit, and put paying for goods and services at your own risk."
      }
